<article class="env-lemma" id="03JN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03JN">Lemma <span data-tag="03JN">68.3.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $Y \to X$ be a representable morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $U \to X$ be a morphism from a scheme to $X$. If the fibres of $U \to X$ are universally bounded, then the fibres of $U \times _ X Y \to Y$ are universally bounded. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is clear from the definition, and properties of fibre products. (Note that $U \times _ X Y$ is a scheme as we assumed $Y \to X$ representable, so the definition applies.) 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>